## Early September Nail Ideas (Still-Summer Vibes)

The first two weeks of September call for a manicure that has not fully let go of summer, and that restraint is the whole point. Early <strong>september nails</strong> are less about committing to fall and more about easing toward it, since a too-early commitment reads try-hard against sun-warmed skin and open-toe sandals still in weekend rotation.

Lean into warmth without darkness. A honey-toned nude with a glossy finish works as a near-universal option, flattering on every undertone and dressy enough for a first-day-back outfit without shouting for attention. Sheer berry jelly, the kind that lets a little of the natural nail show through, gives a soft flush of colour that photographs beautifully against a lingering tan. For anyone wanting more movement, a soft blue-to-nude ombre keeps a summer-adjacent brightness while easing toward the season's cooler undertones.

