Tortoiseshell nail art recreates the mottled brown, amber, and black pattern of the material itself, painted or stamped directly onto the nail in irregular, organic patches rather than a symmetrical print. It reads instantly as autumn without needing a dark base colour, which makes it one of the more forgiving techniques for anyone easing into the season gradually.

Cat-eye gel polish is a magnetic-infused gel formula that, once cured under a magnet, creates a shifting, light-catching line down the centre of the nail similar to the mineral effect in cat's-eye gemstones. Over a jewel-toned base like sapphire or emerald, it gives real dimension without any hand-painted art at all, which explains its popularity with anyone booking a salon appointment rather than doing their own nails. For more on how sapphire and jewel-tone pairings work across the whole September palette, the guide to <a href='/blog/september/september-birthstone-nails'>september birthstone nails</a> covers the stone-inspired angle in more detail.

