## Best Nail Shapes for September

Almond and squoval both work exceptionally well for <strong>september nails</strong>, almond for its slightly softer, more elongating line, squoval for its lower-maintenance, everyday practicality. Neither shape fights against the season's in-between mood the way something more extreme, like a long stiletto or a sharp square edge, tends to.

Almond nails taper gently toward a rounded point, giving fingers a naturally elongated look without the length or fragility of a full stiletto shape. It suits nearly every one of the colours and textures covered above, and it photographs particularly well with aura and tortoiseshell designs since the tapered tip gives gradient effects somewhere natural to fade toward.

