## How Long Will Your September Manicure Last

A well-applied fall gel manicure typically lasts two to three weeks before noticeable regrowth or lifting sets in, which conveniently maps almost exactly onto the runway of September itself. That timing is part of why this season rewards committing to one of these looks rather than half-measuring a quick polish change.

Longevity comes down more to prep than to the specific shade chosen. Clean, fully dry nails, a proper cuticle push-back, and a quality base coat all matter more than whether the finish is matte or glossy. Darker fall tones, burgundy and espresso especially, tend to hide the early signs of wear better than pale or sheer shades, which is one reason they read as more forgiving for anyone who cannot get to a touch-up appointment every two weeks.


